+# To the session on `codex/security-findings-2026-08-13` (beep-effect7)
+
+The publish hold is lifted — PRs #673 (turbo-cache infra activation) and #674
+(CI cache consumption) are merged, along with #672 (Effect 4.0.0-rc.108) and
+#676. You may publish, with the following required sequencing so nothing
+breaks.
+
+## Before anything else
+
+1. `git fetch origin && git merge origin/main` (merge, not rebase — repo
+   norm), then `bun install` — #672 moved the lockfile; skipping the install
+   produces phantom failures.
+2. Expect merge conflicts in files we both touched:
+   - `infra/src/CiTurboCache.ts` — main now removes the `POST /v8/artifacts`
+     route/integration entirely, adds stage throttling, reserved concurrency,
+     and a `loadCiTurboCacheConfig` loader. Keep both sides: your CSF-013
+     invoke-ARN correction applies to the two surviving integrations
+     (read + write); if any hunk of yours references the removed
+     `query-artifact` integration, drop that hunk.
+   - `infra/test/CiTurboCache.test.ts` — same file changed on main; re-apply
+     your Pulumi-mock assertions on top.
+   - `packages/tooling/tool/cli/src/commands/Quality/internal/CoverageRegression.ts`
+     and `standards/coverage.regression-baseline.jsonc` — main merged a new
+     floor for `@beep/repo-docgen` today. If your work regenerates or
+     migrates the baseline, regenerate it ON THE POST-MERGE TREE; never
+     resolve that file by keeping your pre-merge version.
+3. Regenerate every ratchet/baseline artifact you touched on the merged tree
+   before verifying (same rule as above, generally).
+
+## CI environment changes you inherit
+
+- PR lanes now consume the remote turbo cache read-only (`TURBO_*` env is
+  set); fork-style degradation is env-gated and none of it needs anything
+  from you.
+- The Effect CLI and docgen bins now exit explicitly on success — the
+  "lane prints success then hangs/SIGABRTs" class is fixed. If you saw that
+  during earlier verifies, do not chase it; it is gone on merged main.
+
+## Deployment boundary (important)
+
+Your CSF-013 change corrects the API Gateway integrations to the invoke ARN.
+The live stack currently runs the function-ARN form and is probe-proven
+working, so: land the PR, but do NOT run `pulumi up` from your session. The
+operator/infra session deploys it afterward as a two-resource in-place update
+followed by the live probe matrix.
+
+## Publishing shape
+
+Publish as narrow standalone PRs, not one omnibus, in this order of value:
+CSF-002 (legacy runner-launcher retirement) first, then CSF-007 (public
+provenance) and CSF-010 (agent defaults + AI-sync enforcement). Hold
+CSF-009 and CSF-012 until their known gaps are closed (CSF-012: the
+aggregate-flat file-replacement case; also evict the unrelated
+`EffectTsgoEffectFnPolicy.test.ts` edit from the security scope), and keep
+the six runner-admission findings unpublished — they become acceptance
+evidence for the CI architecture work, not fixes claimable now. If your
+newer work (your QUALITY_REVIEW.md) already closes those gaps, say so in
+the PR bodies.
+
+Mechanics: every changed package needs a changeset; commit subjects are
+conventional and lowercase; body lines under 100 chars; publish through
+`bun run beep yeet verify` then publish, and describe each change in the PR
+body in precise, neutral engineering terms (what is validated/enforced,
+which finding id it closes).
