+# Friction receipts pending ledger entry (closeout PR carries these)
+
+Source: the 608-conflict-resolution subagent's reflection (2026-08-08, merge
+of origin/main into feat/jsdoc-carrier-migration-p3, commits `ad15631803` +
+`0b0703e355`). Held here because goals/ files were owned by in-flight PRs at
+capture time; fold into `goals/speed-loop/research/OPPORTUNITIES.md` in the
+closeout PR.
+
+1. **Generated-file auto-merge is wrong in both directions — third confirmed
+   instance.** `goals/INDEX.md` regenerated to 122 packets / 33 active; HEAD
+   said 31, main said 34 — taking EITHER side commits a wrong index.
+   Prevention: a git merge driver marking `goals/INDEX.md`,
+   `standards/jsdoc-*.inventory.*`, and `standards/*.regression-baseline.jsonc`
+   as `merge=regenerate` so conflicts fail loudly instead of auto-merging
+   plausibly-wrong content.
+
+2. **A docs-only codemod branch carried a latent compile break.** The P3
+   branch pinned `S.TaggedErrorClass`; main's effect beta.104 bump renamed
+   the export to `S.TaggedError` (verified: zero occurrences of the old name
+   in the installed package). No gate on the branch itself could catch it
+   before merge — the API simply no longer existed. Prevention: merge main
+   into long-running codemod branches early and often (and ledger #84's
+   merged-tree verify tier is exactly the local gate that would have caught
+   it).
+
+3. **The jsdoc ratchet compares counts only, so it cannot detect a stale
+   inventory.** A concurrent writer shipped an inventory with line anchors
+   from a pre-merge tree (`Id.ts` `make` at 2043 vs actual 2065); totals
+   matched, gate stayed green. Anchors/`generatedAt` are load-bearing for
+   docs tooling but unguarded. Prevention: ratchet check-mode should verify a
+   sample of anchors against the working tree, or hash the anchored spans.
+
+4. **`jsdoc-inventory` costs ~5 min per run (303s/319s observed) and
+   merge-resolution loops run it repeatedly** (three times across two merges
+   here). Prevention: a `--since`-style bounded mode like `docgen:local`,
+   scoped to origin/main...HEAD + dirty files.
+
+Also observed this session (mine, not the subagent's):
+
+5. **Prebuilt-binary download timeout converts to a red lane via a latent
+   env gap** (PR #626, Codegen Drift, 2026-08-08): keytar (transitive via
+   `@azure/msal-node-extensions`) hit "prebuild-install warn install Request
+   timed out", fell back to node-gyp source build, and died on missing
+   `libsecret-1-dev` on the free ubuntu-24.04 runner. Immediate: rerun-once
+   (dispatched); fingerprint added to the #89 scope (install-step infra
+   failure, jobs-API detectable). Durable: the ci-fleet-endgame baked-AMI
+   toolbelt must include `libsecret-1-dev` (and the free-lane setup composite
+   can add it if the class recurs) so the source fallback simply works.
+
+6. **The lane janitor's allowlist lives in a session-scoped scratchpad path**
+   (`/tmp/claude-1000/.../6ac248be.../scratchpad/lane-allowlist.txt`), which a
+   successor session had to rediscover by find(1). Prevention: ops state that
+   outlives a session belongs in a durable repo-adjacent location (the
+   `beep runners` porcelain should own lane-closure state).
